# Fault F10 (W-A): a decision instance with a hole day made every place's balance a hole from the run's start. E §4.1
# step 2: "A hole day or `when` makes a hole movement (LANGUAGE §5.14)"; E §4.2 Holes in the walk: "A hole movement
# makes both ends' balances holes from its day on, with its questions ... Results about earlier days, and about other
# places, stand." The decision p (day d, a hole) moves from x to w: x's balance is the hole d (a); y, which p never
# touches, stands at its plan's 10.00 DUK, and so do g's flows.
=== m.tally
model t10
  tally 2
  on 2026-03-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source src "s"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
place x: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place y: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place w: outside lives 2000-01-01..
input d: date question "when?"
input e: date
input amt: money DUK
move p: transfers
  on d
  reads x
  leg cash from x to w amount max(0, bal(x))
move f: transfers
  on e
  leg cash from w to x amount amt
move g: transfers
  on e
  leg cash from w to y amount amt
ask a: bal(x, 2026-01-31), bal(y, 2026-01-31), flows(g, 2026-01)
version v
  cite src
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[x] = 0.00 DUK at 2026-01-01 start "o"
  opening[y] = 0.00 DUK at 2026-01-01 start "o"
  e = 2026-01-10
  amt = 10.00 DUK
=== expect
a: (?"when?" (d), 10.00 DUK, 10.00 DUK)
  unfulfilled: f
  unfulfilled: g
  cut 2026-03-01
